# Frere Jacques as a round, for two guitars (repertoire plan: frere-jacques-round). Your part
# is the first voice: the tune twice through, then a long G while the teacher finishes. The
# teacher's voice starts the same tune two bars after you. Played without words.
# Notes: G = open string 3, A = string 3 fret 2 (finger 2), B = open string 2, C = string 2
# fret 1 (finger 1), D = string 2 fret 3 (finger 3), E = open string 1, and the low D of
# "ding, dang, dong" is the open string 4. Every beat 1 and 3 of the tune is G, B or D, the notes
# of a G chord, which is why the two voices fit together.
title: Frère Jacques (round)
id: frere-jacques-round
composer: Traditional French
source: French round of the 18th century; arranged for two guitars for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (traditional); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 2
tags: round, duet, eighth notes, french
tempo: 96
time: 4/4
key: G

track: You (first voice)
role: lead
[Round]
